{
    "background_story": "Zeke was a rugged fisherman from the small town of Aberdeen, Scotland. He spent his life braving the harsh North Sea, reeling in the day's catch to support his family. Zeke's love for the sea was only matched by his love for his hometown, where his family had lived for generations. He took great pride in Aberdeen's rich history and culture, often regaling his fellow fishermen with tales of the city's medieval past. When the local harbor was threatened by a large development project, Zeke rallied the community to fight for its preservation. His determination and leadership helped save the historic harbor, ensuring that Aberdeen's heritage would be protected for years to come. Zeke's love for his hometown and its people earned him the nickname 'The Aberdeen Anchor'.",
